            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 22-year-old female patient, admitted on 03.08.2026 with acute lower abdominal pain and a positive pregnancy test. Clinical assessment, serum beta-hCG measurement, and transvaginal ultrasound confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy without signs of rupture on initial presentation. Given the clinical findings and hemodynamic stability, the patient was counseled and consented for surgical intervention. She underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy with successful removal of the ectopic pregnancy. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound care was provided, and the patient received appropriate postoperative analgesia and intravenous fluids. She was discharged home on 04.08.2026 in good general condition. Follow-up serum beta-hCG monitoring and contraceptive counseling have been recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
